text:
Reduce size of testings images by default to speed up tests.   Note, this is a bit hacky,
but it should be simple enough to modify the Image class, for example passing in
dimensions and such.   It is unlikely that tests will require multiple testing images, so
there shouldn't be a need to generate multiple different images, but obviously if that
is required, you can change this approach.


Since this defaults to 50x50, the file size (at 100% jpeg compression) is about
650 bytes.

I set it up so you can still generate larger images if you want using pytest markers or
something along those lines.

The key part for this just makes my image smaller...

    @property
    def pil_image(self):
        return PIL.Image.new('RGB', self.dimensions, self.color)

.. to this:

    @property
    def pil_image(self):
        return PIL.Image.new('RGB', self.dimensions, self.color)

I also realized the kept the fixture function:

@pytest.fixture()
def image():
    return Image()

