text:
The function `create` should have all parameters needed to initialize InlineKeyboardButton, like
`text`, `url`, `callback_data`, `switch_inline_query`. It can be used to create an instance of this class with a one call.
The easiest way to use it is when you need to create just one InlineKeyboardButton. But if you need to create multiple InlineKeyboardButtons with just changing some parameters, it's better to use it in the following way:

```python
button = InlineKeyboardButton.create("Button text", url="...")
another_button = button.create("Another text", another_url="...")
```

```python
on the fly:
button = InlineKeyboardButton.create
You can make a local copy of it if you're not using it in other classes:
button = InlineKeyboardButton.create
```

